<title>UK: Euro vacuum gas oil in doldrums ahead of holidays.</title>
<headline>Euro vacuum gas oil in doldrums ahead of holidays.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>bid/ask	prev bid/ask</p>
<p> Low sulphur cargoes fob NWE	  163/165	  163/165</p>
<p> High sulphur cargoes fob NWE	 149/151	  149/151</p>
<p> High sulphur barges fob ARA	  156/157	  156/157</p>
<p> Formula quotation fob Med	     08/12	    08/12</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The European vacuum gas oil market was quiet ahead of the holiday break with little activity seen.</p>
<p>Deals have mainly focussed on barges which have been done at quotes-related numbers.</p>
<p>&quot;Cargo business is limited at the moment,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Although easier prices earlier in the week shut the arbitrage to the U.S., at least one low sulphur cargo was expected to head transatlantic.</p>
<p>&quot;The arb can sometimes be squeezed open, but this cargo may have to take a hit,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
